Cap WebServer raw upload reads to the remaining content length so the final
partial chunk does not wait the full 5 s WiFiClient timeout.

ESP32 Arduino WebServer's raw upload loop calls
  client.readBytes(buf, HTTP_RAW_BUFLEN /* 1436 */)
on every iteration. When the remaining bytes are smaller than HTTP_RAW_BUFLEN
(almost always true on the last chunk), readBytes blocks waiting for bytes that
will never arrive, until HTTP_MAX_SEND_WAIT (5000 ms) elapses. This adds a
fixed ~5 second tail to every audio POST regardless of payload size.

The fix caps the read request to the actual remaining bytes so readBytes
returns immediately once it has read the last byte.

Target file (system package, not in this repository):
  ~/.platformio/packages/framework-arduinoespressif32/libraries/WebServer/src/Parsing.cpp

Applied automatically at build time by scripts/apply_webserver_patch.py.
Apply manually with:
  patch -p0 -d <framework dir>/libraries/WebServer/src < patches/webserver_raw_read_cap.patch

--- Parsing.cpp.orig
+++ Parsing.cpp
@@ -184,7 +184,12 @@
       _currentRaw->status = RAW_WRITE;

       while (_currentRaw->totalSize < _clientContentLength) {
-        _currentRaw->currentSize = client.readBytes(_currentRaw->buf, HTTP_RAW_BUFLEN);
+        // PATCH(minimum-headroom): cap readBytes() to remaining bytes so the
+        // final partial chunk does not wait the full 5s WiFiClient timeout.
+        size_t toRead = HTTP_RAW_BUFLEN;
+        size_t remaining = _clientContentLength - _currentRaw->totalSize;
+        if (remaining < toRead) toRead = remaining;
+        _currentRaw->currentSize = client.readBytes(_currentRaw->buf, toRead);
         _currentRaw->totalSize += _currentRaw->currentSize;
         if (_currentRaw->currentSize == 0) {
           _currentRaw->status = RAW_ABORTED;
